course: dictionary
lesson: 13784
title: Words for what is inside
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what something is really like, deep down. «Intrinsic» is one of them. It means belonging to the real nature of something itself, not something added on from outside.
explain: «A square has four equal sides. Those sides are intrinsic to a square.» The sides are not a decoration or a label. A shape without them would not be a square, so the sides belong to what a square really is.
explain: Read the words around intrinsic for clues. «Ruby paints because she loves it, not for a prize.» Her reason comes from inside her, so her motivation is intrinsic. Ask yourself: is this part of the thing itself, or does it come from outside? That question will often find the meaning.
fact: Intrinsic is a formal adjective, so you will mostly meet it in serious writing.
fact: «Intrinsic» means belonging to the real nature of something itself.
fact: «Intrinsic value» means value that a thing has in itself, not because of what someone else gives it.
fact: «Intrinsic motivation» means doing something because you enjoy it, not because you want a reward.
fact: «Intrinsic to» means being a basic part of something: «Curiosity is intrinsic to scientists.»
exercise: «A square has four equal sides. Those sides are intrinsic to a square.» What does intrinsic mean here? | Very large | Broken or damaged | Added on from outside later | *Part of the real nature of the thing
exercise: Ruby paints because she loves it, not for a prize. Her motivation is intrinsic. What kind of motivation is this? | Doing it because someone ordered her to | Doing it by accident | Doing it only to win a reward | *Doing it because she enjoys it
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you the value belongs to the ring itself: «The gold ring has intrinsic value.» | value | *intrinsic | gold | ring
test: «Kindness is intrinsic to a good friend.» What does intrinsic to mean here? | Something a friend forgets | Something a friend buys from a shop | *Part of what a good friend really is | Something that happens only on birthdays
test: Why is intrinsic motivation different from working for a prize? | *It comes from enjoying the task itself | It comes from a reward you get at the end | It comes from a teacher who is watching | It comes from being told to do it
exam: Which sentence uses intrinsic correctly? | My shoes are intrinsic because I bought them in town. | The score was intrinsic, because the teacher gave it to me. | The prize was intrinsic, and it came in the post. | *Curiosity is intrinsic to young scientists.
